title: 'Fold extrinsic length into the `proof_size` weight dimension before the extension pipeline'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The FRAME `Executive` now adds the encoded extrinsic length to the `proof_size` dimension of
      `dispatch_info.call_weight` before running the transaction-extension pipeline. As a result
      `DispatchInfo::total_weight()` already accounts for the extrinsic length as part of the
      storage proof, and transaction extensions no longer need to add the length manually for
      `proof_size` accounting (`CheckWeight` no longer does so either).

      Block length enforcement (`CheckWeight::check_block_length`) is unchanged and still uses the
      raw extrinsic length. The storage-weight-reclaim logic (both
      `cumulus-pallet-weight-reclaim` and `cumulus-primitives-storage-weight-reclaim`) treats the
      extrinsic length as non-reclaimable proof size, so it is always kept in the block weight and
      never reclaimed.

      `frame_system::Pallet::reclaim_weight` gained an `extrinsic_len` parameter; callers that used
      the deprecated `CheckWeight::do_post_dispatch` are unaffected.

      Closes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/9410.
  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      The extrinsic length is now part of the `proof_size` weight dimension. On runtimes whose
      `pallet_transaction_payment::Config::WeightToFee` prices the `proof_size` dimension (for
      example `pallet_revive::evm::fees::BlockRatioFee`, used by Asset Hub), the extrinsic length
      now contributes to the weight-based fee in addition to the existing `LengthToFee` charge.
      Runtimes that do not price `proof_size` in `WeightToFee` (the common `ref_time`-only case)
      are unaffected.

crates:
  - name: frame-executive
    bump: patch
  - name: frame-system
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-pallet-weight-reclaim
    bump: patch
  - name: cumulus-primitives-storage-weight-reclaim
    bump: patch
